            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "schnoodlemom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of our family favorites and one we make often. One thing I have learned is to put all the dressing ingredients in the blender and puree' instead of trying to finely chop the onion and wisk everything together. MUCH easier! In the winter time when strawberries are out of season (or just for a change), I use a can or two of mandarin oranges instead of strawberries. Crumbled feta cheese is also good on this salad if you like feta and crushed walnuts are a good (and cheaper) substitute for the almonds if you don't have almonds on hand. Thanks for the recipe!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "UZIMIKE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This recipe was a big winner. Small modifications to the original:\n\nCut the sugar down to ¼ cup.\nAdd a few turns of fresh ground pepper\nUse balsamic vinegar.\nUse red onion.\nAdd some fresh bacon bits\nAdd a mix of blue cheese and feta cheese.\nAlso, do not mix the dressing in with greens, as it will only wilt the salad. Just apply as normal dressing. Mixing in the dressing and letting it sit I think would make it too ‘limpy’. \n\nWe put a few red onion slices on top with the cheese and bacon. It was great. The sweetness of the dressing would have been excessively much at ½ cup of sugar. This we will make again and again and again.",
            "datePublished": "2006-04-12T08:04:57.997Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "blys"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great but substitue balsamic vinegar for white, purple onions instead of white then add blueberries and bananas to the strawberries and it's to die for.",
            "datePublished": "2006-08-08T13:11:41.827Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JazzyBacon8946"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Lightly toast the almonds instead of blanching them. Use dried minced onions. Make the dressing in a mason jar and shake as needed You can also reduce the sugar without affecting taste",
            "datePublished": "2024-03-22T20:27:43.448Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this many times. I cut the sugar back in the dressing to 3 Tbsp's which gave it a wonderful contrast of sweet and sharp. I also used blanched sliced almonds and candied them to add the sweetness missing in the dressing and a little crunch to the salad. Rave reviews from co-workers and family.",
            "datePublished": "2023-10-03T06:34:12.075Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MMAtlanta"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 3 tbs of sugar, 1/3 cup olive oil and balsamic vinegar. No leftovers! IMO, this produces more than 4 servings unless this is a large part of your meal.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-30T13:52:15.797Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chef 'Chelle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made this recipe many times. Have started adding feta cheese and diced chicken to make as a nice summer meal with deviled eggs on the side. \nMy time saving way of making this is by warming vinegar in a jar to help dissolve the sugar. Grate the onion with a cheese grater for less cleanup, mix dressing by shaking in the jar, and then can easily store leftover w/o dirtying another dish.\nThank you for sharing this wonderful recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2019-05-08T12:40:19.850Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jessie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved this recipe. I committed the cardinal sin of changing some of the recipe, but that tells me that the recipe is very forgiving. I cut back the sugar and oil in the dressing, added canned mandarin oranges, thinly sliced red onion, blue cheese, and honey roasted nuts. Thanks to everyone who contributed to making this a great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-06T23:53:41.998Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angela HJ"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was absolutely delicious! I made some changes based on the reviews and what I had on hand. Used balsamic vinegar, made candied walnuts following another reviewers suggestion (mixed together egg white, sugar, cinnamon, nutmeg, then added walnuts, baked until golden), added blueberries &amp; blue cheese . . . awesome salad that even my kids loved.",
            "datePublished": "2021-03-22T02:31:45.350Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SwiftPea5226"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Delicious basic salad that can be tweaked in multiple ways! During the summer, I love to serve this with grilled chicken and red onion. My family also likes to add a little bit of goat cheese as well.",
            "datePublished": "2024-04-08T22:26:31.099Z"
          },
